<i> when I completely imploded
and crashed my brains out.</i>


00:49:56.359 --> 00:49:57.717
<i> That was when
we got introduced,</i>


00:49:57.717 --> 00:49:59.116
<i> and here we were a year later</i>


00:49:59.116 --> 00:50:00.754
<i> and she was in my corner,</i>


00:50:00.754 --> 00:50:03.871
<i> and she was the one there
giving me my medal.</i>


00:50:03.871 --> 00:50:05.509
<i>For Hart,
the trick was behind him,</i>


00:50:05.509 --> 00:50:06.987
<i>and Metzger found himself again</i>


00:50:06.987 --> 00:50:08.905
<i>at the forefront of the sport,</i>


00:50:08.905 --> 00:50:10.145
<i> but for every other rider,</i>


00:50:10.145 --> 00:50:11.263
<i> it was flip</i>


00:50:11.263 --> 00:50:13.262
<i> or your career was over.</i>


00:50:13.262 --> 00:50:14.660
From that point on,


00:50:14.660 --> 00:50:16.859
the backflip became reality,


00:50:16.859 --> 00:50:17.897
and it was something


00:50:17.897 --> 00:50:20.814
that became freestyle motocross,


00:50:20.814 --> 00:50:23.251
and that everybody
had to conquer


00:50:23.251 --> 00:50:25.090
<i> in order to become</i>


00:50:25.090 --> 00:50:27.607
<i> the top level of the sport.</i>


00:50:27.607 --> 00:50:29.125
Even if you did
a hundred of them,


00:50:29.125 --> 00:50:30.245
that one you don't pull,


00:50:30.245 --> 00:50:31.564
you're done, you know.


00:50:31.564 --> 00:50:33.362
And I just didn't want
any part of it.


00:50:36.119 --> 00:50:38.077
This is something
everyone is gonna have to learn


00:50:38.077 --> 00:50:39.556
if you wanna be relevant
in the game


00:50:39.556 --> 00:50:40.635
of freestyle motocross,


00:50:40.635 --> 00:50:41.953
game changer.


00:50:45.471 --> 00:50:47.508
<i>Even Brian Deegan,
a top competitor,</i>


00:50:47.508 --> 00:50:49.266
<i> struggled with the backflip.</i>


00:50:49.266 --> 00:50:51.145
<i> As Carey Hart proved,
going inverted</i>


00:50:51.145 --> 00:50:53.582
<i>means more severe consequences.</i>


00:50:53.582 --> 00:50:55.660
<i> Athletes,
many well established,</i>


00:50:55.660 --> 00:50:58.297
<i> like Clifford "The Flyin'
Hawaiian" Adoptante,</i>


00:50:58.297 --> 00:51:00.215
<i> Tommy "Tom Cat" Clowers,</i>


00:51:00.215 --> 00:51:02.374
<i> and the Smooth Drake McElroy,</i>


00:51:02.374 --> 00:51:04.172
<i> began disappearing
from the scene.</i>


00:51:04.172 --> 00:51:05.450
Man, like,
"Dude, am I done?


00:51:05.450 --> 00:51:06.729
Am I--never get a medal again?"


00:51:06.729 --> 00:51:08.807
And, "What am I gonna do?"


00:51:08.807 --> 00:51:10.406
<i> Oh, the backflip don't work.</i>


00:51:10.406 --> 00:51:11.964
<i> And this is something
that we're gonna be doing</i>


00:51:11.964 --> 00:51:13.842
<i> all the time, have down.</i>


00:51:13.842 --> 00:51:15.400
Do tricks
while we're upside-down,


00:51:15.400 --> 00:51:19.078
and just beat that was,
it's gonna happen.


00:51:19.078 --> 00:51:21.715
<i> But when the backflip
came about,</i>


00:51:21.715 --> 00:51:24.832
there's a lot of guys
that just packed it up.


00:51:27.029 --> 00:51:28.309
I don't think
there's any other sport


00:51:28.309 --> 00:51:31.465
on the planet
that pushes progression


00:51:31.465 --> 00:51:34.262
and risk as hard as we do.


00:51:34.262 --> 00:51:36.461
<i> What other sport in
the Olympics has had a new move</i>


00:51:36.461 --> 00:51:38.459
<i> invented since when?</i>


00:51:38.459 --> 00:51:40.657
You tell me.
Is this--is there a new--


00:51:40.657 --> 00:51:42.494
is there a new, you know,
do they got some new,


00:51:42.494 --> 00:51:44.493
uh, obstacles in the gym?


00:51:44.493 --> 00:51:46.451
I don't think people
really quantitized


00:51:46.451 --> 00:51:48.848
how much effort
goes in to what,


00:51:48.848 --> 00:51:50.567
you know,
what these guys are doing.


00:51:50.567 --> 00:51:51.885
<i> Probably one
of the toughest things</i>


00:51:51.885 --> 00:51:53.724
I ever had to do,
learning the flip back,


00:51:53.724 --> 00:51:55.202
decided to go for it.


00:51:55.202 --> 00:51:56.961
<i> I probably hesitated
with my throttle.</i>


00:51:56.961 --> 00:51:58.558
<i> I just didn't have it
panned off the ramp,</i>


00:51:58.558 --> 00:52:01.676
<i> my body positioning
wasn't right.</i>


00:52:01.676 --> 00:52:04.473
The whole thing was just
extremely embarrassing for me.


00:52:04.473 --> 00:52:06.192
And that was pretty
much like the last time


00:52:06.192 --> 00:52:07.950
you've seen
a lot of dudes compete,


00:52:07.950 --> 00:52:10.268
because they didn't want
to backflip anymore.


00:52:10.268 --> 00:52:13.584
<i> All I had to do
was the flip and I was in.</i>


00:52:13.584 --> 00:52:16.502
<i> Big contracts would come,
my life would be easy,</i>


00:52:16.502 --> 00:52:18.939
I would get paid to ride,
my dream would come true.


00:52:18.939 --> 00:52:21.816
<i> I think I was just
in major denial.</i>


00:52:21.816 --> 00:52:23.614
Deep down inside
I knew I was done.


00:52:25.612 --> 00:52:27.052
<i> With the loss of so much talent,</i>


00:52:27.052 --> 00:52:28.970
<i> the door was left open
for newcomers,</i>


00:52:28.970 --> 00:52:31.727
<i> groomed on riding ramps
and practicing tricks.</i>


00:52:31.727 --> 00:52:33.525
<i> Nate Adams
did master the backflip</i>


00:52:33.525 --> 00:52:35.683
<i> and started dominating
competitions.</i>


00:52:35.683 --> 00:52:38.960
<i>Not to be outdone, Brian Deegan
mastered the flip as well.</i>


00:52:38.960 --> 00:52:41.597
<i> But the Godfather of FMX,
Mike Metzger,</i>


00:52:41.597 --> 00:52:44.475
<i>had it so dialed that he wanted
to push it further.</i>


00:52:50.828 --> 00:52:52.986
<i> It was his idea that,
"Hey, you know what?</i>


00:52:52.986 --> 00:52:54.585
<i> We're daredevils.</i>


00:52:54.585 --> 00:52:56.223
<i> Why don't we follow
in the footsteps of,</i>


00:52:56.223 --> 00:52:58.381
you know, the greatest
daredevil of all,


00:52:58.381 --> 00:53:00.859
Evel Knievel?"


00:53:00.859 --> 00:53:02.577
Mission Impossible
wants to do a big stunt.


00:53:02.577 --> 00:53:04.494
They wanna re jump over
Caesar's Palace fountain.


00:53:04.494 --> 00:53:06.133
<i> So I called Mike Metzger.</i>


00:53:06.133 --> 00:53:07.811
Accomplished.


00:53:07.811 --> 00:53:10.449
Mike goes, "I am in.
What do I have to do?"


00:53:10.449 --> 00:53:12.206
So, Mike's moving
freestyle in a completely


00:53:12.206 --> 00:53:13.646
different direction now.


00:53:13.646 --> 00:53:16.083
He's got his fame.
People know this guy


00:53:16.083 --> 00:53:19.400
and now he's going to do
this gigantic backflip


00:53:19.400 --> 00:53:22.118
over the fountains
that Evel Knievel


00:53:22.118 --> 00:53:24.236
attempted many years before.


00:53:28.272 --> 00:53:31.309
<i> I never really looked
at myself as a stunt guy.</i>


00:53:31.309 --> 00:53:33.547
I looked at myself as
a professional motorcycle rider,


00:53:33.547 --> 00:53:35.025
so...


00:53:35.025 --> 00:53:38.702
I knew that doing
this record jump,


00:53:38.702 --> 00:53:39.740
I was gonna practice.


00:53:39.740 --> 00:53:41.140
<i> Now comes the testing.</i>


00:53:41.140 --> 00:53:42.858
<i> So, the execs
from Paramount come.</i>


00:53:42.858 --> 00:53:44.377
Guys fly in from Bristol.


00:53:44.377 --> 00:53:46.734
The ESPN guys,
camera crew is there,


00:53:46.734 --> 00:53:48.093
I'm waiting there,


00:53:48.093 --> 00:53:49.892
standing in this giant
massive structure


00:53:49.892 --> 00:53:51.848
that's been built in this--
in this yard.


00:53:51.848 --> 00:53:54.446
Probably it was about
50 feet tall,


00:53:54.446 --> 00:53:55.804
the scaffolding landing


00:53:55.804 --> 00:53:57.363
that wasn't covered


00:53:57.363 --> 00:53:58.921
by any drapery.


00:53:58.921 --> 00:54:00.839
It was just like this big,


00:54:00.839 --> 00:54:03.876
huge colossal rods and bars,


00:54:03.876 --> 00:54:07.474
and it was basically
the replica


00:54:07.474 --> 00:54:10.151
of how the whole setup
was gonna be


00:54:10.151 --> 00:54:11.470
at Caesar's.


00:54:11.470 --> 00:54:13.069
I had nightmares running
through my head of


00:54:13.069 --> 00:54:16.185
if I have a problem
with my bike,


00:54:16.185 --> 00:54:18.064
something malfunctioned,


00:54:18.064 --> 00:54:19.542
I'm gonna end up disintegrating


00:54:19.542 --> 00:54:21.141
myself like a cheese grater


00:54:21.141 --> 00:54:23.618
through this deal.


00:54:23.618 --> 00:54:24.657
<i> Metzger comes.</i>


00:54:24.657 --> 00:54:25.895
<i> Drives past everybody,</i>


00:54:25.895 --> 00:54:27.335
<i> walks up on the runway,</i>


00:54:27.335 --> 00:54:29.173
points at me, he says,
"Come here, Taublieb."


00:54:29.173 --> 00:54:30.412
So, I walk up there,
everybody's looking up,


00:54:30.412 --> 00:54:31.890
"What's going on?"


00:54:31.890 --> 00:54:33.249
<i> And the best scenario
in my head</i>


00:54:33.249 --> 00:54:35.647
<i> was to tell him
I forgot my helmet.</i>


00:54:35.647 --> 00:54:37.164
It was a lie.
I had my helmet.


00:54:37.164 --> 00:54:38.762
It was stashed in my truck.
I just didn't feel


00:54:38.762 --> 00:54:40.640
like jumping that day.


00:54:40.640 --> 00:54:42.679
<i> The job at hand was to,</i>


00:54:42.679 --> 00:54:45.476
basically, turn off my mind,


00:54:45.476 --> 00:54:47.154
and my emotions,


00:54:47.154 --> 00:54:49.033
and come back the following day,


00:54:49.033 --> 00:54:50.471
and handle it.


00:54:53.189 --> 00:54:55.266
Mike Metzger came to that yard


00:54:55.266 --> 00:54:56.786
at 8 o'clock in the morning,


00:54:56.786 --> 00:54:58.545
with no ambulance, no people,


00:54:58.545 --> 00:55:00.063
<i> no camera, and he started,</i>


00:55:00.063 --> 00:55:01.821
<i> he had hit that ramp
before we got there.</i>


00:55:14.609 --> 00:55:16.647
He's backflipped, but
I purposely don't measure it.


00:55:16.647 --> 00:55:18.206
We kind of roughly do it,
'cause I don't wanna


00:55:18.206 --> 00:55:20.483
officially set the record.


00:55:20.483 --> 00:55:22.441
I put my bike in the garage


00:55:22.441 --> 00:55:24.637
and I didn't even start my bike
until a week later


00:55:24.637 --> 00:55:27.116
when I showed up to Vegas.


00:55:27.116 --> 00:55:29.034
<i> What better way
to celebrate 40 years</i>


00:55:29.034 --> 00:55:30.632
<i> of Caesar's Palace history</i>


00:55:30.632 --> 00:55:32.711
<i> than with a high risk feat
that promises</i>


00:55:32.711 --> 00:55:34.029
<i> to take your breath away.</i>


00:55:34.029 --> 00:55:35.667
<i> A world record try</i>


00:55:35.667 --> 00:55:38.664
<i> with a Guinness World Record
representative on hand</i>


00:55:38.664 --> 00:55:40.623
<i>for longest backflip attempted</i>


00:55:40.623 --> 00:55:42.061
<i> by the most influential rider</i>


00:55:42.061 --> 00:55:43.620
<i> in Freestyle Motocross.</i>


00:55:45.977 --> 00:55:48.135
<i> It was pretty
nerve-racking for me</i>


00:55:48.135 --> 00:55:49.855
<i> because it got windy.</i>


00:55:49.855 --> 00:55:51.732
Started--the wind started
picking up.


00:55:51.732 --> 00:55:52.971
<i> Just the bad stuff
that happened there</i>


00:55:52.971 --> 00:55:54.330
<i> with Evel Knievel,</i>


00:55:54.330 --> 00:55:56.009
<i> pillaging himself,
and he's lucky</i>


00:55:56.009 --> 00:55:57.807
<i> he didn't die that time.</i>


00:55:57.807 --> 00:55:59.805
And I was pretty worried
about that.


00:55:59.805 --> 00:56:01.802
<i> I was afraid for Mike,
because I--</i>


00:56:01.802 --> 00:56:03.242
he looked nervous to me


00:56:03.242 --> 00:56:04.800
and I've never seen him
look nervous before.


00:56:04.800 --> 00:56:06.319
<i> I had this vision
that he was going to,</i>


00:56:06.319 --> 00:56:08.316
<i> uh, over rotate it</i>


00:56:08.316 --> 00:56:10.434
and because he was so hyped up,


00:56:10.434 --> 00:56:12.632
and really take a bad fall.


00:56:12.632 --> 00:56:15.309
<i> I had told the ESPN
people how I was gonna do it,</i>


00:56:15.309 --> 00:56:17.068
basically scope the ramp up,


00:56:17.068 --> 00:56:20.344
go back, do two runs
at the ramp and,


00:56:20.344 --> 00:56:22.382
<i>as soon as I took the cape off
I was gonna rip.</i>


00:56:22.382 --> 00:56:24.820
<i> I think we're all worried
about the wind conditions here</i>


00:56:24.820 --> 00:56:26.698
<i>because on Las Vegas Boulevard,</i>


00:56:26.698 --> 00:56:28.656
<i> the hotels here
make their own valley,</i>


00:56:28.656 --> 00:56:29.815
<i> the wind can swirl.</i>


00:56:32.852 --> 00:56:34.371
<i> Guys, here we go.
This could be it.</i>


00:56:34.371 --> 00:56:35.609
<i> The impossible jump.</i>


00:56:38.326 --> 00:56:40.726
I hit the ramp faster
and, in the air,


00:56:40.726 --> 00:56:42.443
I started to over rotate.


00:56:55.590 --> 00:56:57.068
<i> Mission accomplished.</i>


00:56:57.068 --> 00:56:59.906
<i> Mike Metzger
has set a World Record</i>


00:56:59.906 --> 00:57:02.783
<i> for Longest Backflip Jump.</i>


00:57:05.460 --> 00:57:07.258
<i> As soon as I hit
wheel to wheel,</i>


00:57:07.258 --> 00:57:09.696
I was like "Dude, that was
for sure the biggest flip


00:57:09.696 --> 00:57:11.095
I've ever done."


00:57:13.333 --> 00:57:15.090
I just thought,
he looked so natural at it.


00:57:15.090 --> 00:57:17.209
He did it so perfect.
He made it look like,


00:57:17.209 --> 00:57:18.887
"Ha, nothing.
That was nothing."


00:57:20.766 --> 00:57:22.284
<i>Always made riding motorcycles</i>


00:57:22.284 --> 00:57:23.922
<i> look like that to me.</i>


00:57:23.922 --> 00:57:26.919
<i>The Caesar's Fountain
was known for,</i>


00:57:26.919 --> 00:57:29.157
<i> you know, Evel's big attempt</i>


00:57:29.157 --> 00:57:31.037
<i> and massive crash.</i>


00:57:31.037 --> 00:57:34.832
To be a part of his legacy,
it was just, you know,


00:57:34.832 --> 00:57:38.230
a real cool opportunity
that I got to handle.


00:57:38.230 --> 00:57:39.828
Thank you.


00:57:39.828 --> 00:57:41.185
<i>Metzger's record
promoted the sport</i>


00:57:41.185 --> 00:57:42.944
<i> into the minds
of a global audience.</i>


00:57:42.944 --> 00:57:43.903
Thanks for coming.


00:57:45.462 --> 00:57:46.940
<i> Unfortunately, he was injured</i>


00:57:46.940 --> 00:57:49.098
<i> for the next big stage.</i>


00:57:49.098 --> 00:57:52.094
<i> Golden Sunset
at the former Olympic Venue,</i>


00:57:52.094 --> 00:57:53.734
<i> the LA Coliseum.</i>


00:57:53.734 --> 00:57:55.412
<i> Packed with fans,
the rumors had filtered</i>


00:57:55.412 --> 00:57:56.770
<i> through the crowd,</i>


00:57:56.770 --> 00:57:58.848
<i> creating an electric
environment.</i>


00:57:58.848 --> 00:58:01.646
<i> The sport was again
about to go to another level</i>


00:58:01.646 --> 00:58:04.203
<i> with a new terrifying trick.</i>


00:58:04.203 --> 00:58:06.121
<i> From the time X Game ends</i>


00:58:06.121 --> 00:58:07.641
<i> to the time the X Game starts</i>


00:58:07.641 --> 00:58:08.679
that following year,


00:58:08.679 --> 00:58:11.636
you know, there's serious,


00:58:11.636 --> 00:58:13.673
serious training


00:58:13.673 --> 00:58:15.073
and homework going on


00:58:15.073 --> 00:58:16.831
that these athletes put in.


00:58:16.831 --> 00:58:20.308
The rumor is now gone away


00:58:20.308 --> 00:58:21.387
from the backflip.


00:58:21.387 --> 00:58:22.666
It's about something else


00:58:22.666 --> 00:58:24.704
and it's all about
Travis Pastrana


00:58:24.704 --> 00:58:26.583
is gonna do this trick.


00:58:26.583 --> 00:58:28.539
<i>As insane as the backflip was,</i>


00:58:28.539 --> 00:58:31.057
<i> the 360 brought a new
tortured dimension</i>


00:58:31.057 --> 00:58:32.136
<i> to physics,</i>


00:58:32.136 --> 00:58:34.614
<i>whipping a 260-pound motorcycle</i>


00:58:34.614 --> 00:58:36.293
<i> sideways off a ramp,</i>


00:58:36.293 --> 00:58:38.890
<i> flat spinning it off
its natural axis,</i>


00:58:38.890 --> 00:58:40.528
<i> and then finding
forward momentum</i>


00:58:40.528 --> 00:58:41.606
<i> to ride away when it wants</i>


00:58:41.606 --> 00:58:43.365
<i> to throw you sideways.</i>


00:58:43.365 --> 00:58:45.443
<i> We had a whole year
to plan for the X Games.</i>


00:58:45.443 --> 00:58:47.241
So, I go out and we had just
built the foam pit


00:58:47.241 --> 00:58:48.200
and I start working on,


00:58:48.200 --> 00:58:49.279
you know,
trying all these things.


00:58:49.279 --> 00:58:50.518
<i> So, I get out there
and I'm like,</i>


00:58:50.518 --> 00:58:51.598
<i> "I'm gonna land this trick.</i>


00:58:51.598 --> 00:58:52.676
<i> I'm gonna--just the world</i>


00:58:52.676 --> 00:58:53.715
is just--this is--


00:58:53.715 --> 00:58:54.754
it's gonna hit them by storm.


00:58:54.754 --> 00:58:56.352
This is gonna be awesome!"


00:58:56.352 --> 00:58:57.831
<i> Yeah, I hear that
Deegan's got a trick,</i>


00:58:57.831 --> 00:58:59.270
<i> but I haven't really heard
what it is.</i>


00:58:59.270 --> 00:59:00.548
<i> No one really knows,</i>


00:59:00.548 --> 00:59:02.586
<i> but I was online
looking around,</i>


00:59:02.586 --> 00:59:04.424
and I had seen him
doing this, kind of, like,


00:59:04.424 --> 00:59:06.063
360 looking thing at his house.


00:59:06.063 --> 00:59:07.103
And this is why everyone


00:59:07.103 --> 00:59:08.621
is so secretive now with tricks.


00:59:08.621 --> 00:59:10.219
They don't let anyone see it
until X Games


00:59:10.219 --> 00:59:11.858
because--I also was,
kind of, looking at it,


00:59:11.858 --> 00:59:12.936
and studying it,
going, "All right,


00:59:12.936 --> 00:59:14.296
I'm gonna go figure this out."


00:59:16.094 --> 00:59:17.132
<i> I'm in the foam pit</i>


00:59:17.132 --> 00:59:18.531
<i> and I get, honestly,</i>


00:59:18.531 --> 00:59:20.650
<i> probably two or three
out of ten,</i>


00:59:20.650 --> 00:59:21.688
<i> I get around.</i>


00:59:21.688 --> 00:59:22.727
<i> If I really need it,</i>


00:59:22.727 --> 00:59:24.126
<i> it's a 50/50 chance</i>


00:59:24.126 --> 00:59:25.484
<i> I'm gonna land this or,
you know,</i>


00:59:25.484 --> 00:59:27.641
<i> go home in an ambulance.</i>


00:59:30.320 --> 00:59:31.798
<i> Deegan was up first.</i>


00:59:31.798 --> 00:59:34.355
<i> Pastrana and Nate Adams
would follow.</i>


00:59:36.594 --> 00:59:38.432
<i> The largest crowd
in X Games history,</i>


00:59:38.432 --> 00:59:40.150
<i> in excess of 40,000 people</i>


00:59:40.150 --> 00:59:42.828
<i> to see the next competitor
in the finals.</i>


00:59:42.828 --> 00:59:45.025
<i> We missed him in Winter X
due to injury,</i>


00:59:45.025 --> 00:59:46.544
<i> but the Minister of Defense</i>


00:59:46.544 --> 00:59:48.062
<i> for the Metal Mulisha</i>


00:59:48.062 --> 00:59:49.381
<i> is in L.A. now,</i>


00:59:49.381 --> 00:59:51.460
<i> Brian Deegan.</i>


00:59:51.460 --> 00:59:53.577
<i> He needs to nail a good run.
In his first run,</i>


00:59:53.577 --> 00:59:55.015
<i> he kind of stunk up
the place.</i>


00:59:55.015 --> 00:59:56.533
<i> I don't wanna dis him
too hard,</i>


00:59:56.533 --> 00:59:58.373
<i> but he needs to nail it
much harder here...</i>


00:59:58.373 --> 00:59:59.451
<i>Deegan cruised through his run</i>


00:59:59.451 --> 01:00:00.889
<i> with his sights set</i>


01:00:00.889 --> 01:00:03.447
<i> on beating Travis
to the 360 punch.</i>


01:00:03.447 --> 01:00:05.246
I knew it wasn't enough
to win the event


01:00:05.246 --> 01:00:06.285
and I was, kind of, like,


01:00:06.285 --> 01:00:07.843
frustrated and mad.


01:00:07.843 --> 01:00:09.282
<i>Time is winding.</i>


01:00:09.282 --> 01:00:10.680
<i> Time is out.</i>


01:00:10.680 --> 01:00:11.920
<i> Not sure if this kid
accounted--</i>


01:00:11.920 --> 01:00:12.958
<i> is he gonna bust
something new,</i>


01:00:12.958 --> 01:00:14.197
<i> ladies and gentlemen?</i>


01:00:14.197 --> 01:00:15.636
<i> Oh!</i>


01:00:15.636 --> 01:00:17.074
<i> Oh, Deegan!</i>


01:00:17.074 --> 01:00:18.673
<i> He landed a 360!</i>


01:00:18.673 --> 01:00:20.631
<i>Oh, my gosh!</i>


01:00:23.229 --> 01:00:25.306
<i> Brian Deegan has just landed</i>


01:00:25.306 --> 01:00:27.145
<i> the first 360</i>


01:00:27.145 --> 01:00:28.543
<i> on a motorcycle</i>


01:00:28.543 --> 01:00:30.302
<i> ever in the competition.</i>


01:00:30.302 --> 01:00:31.340
He was as surprised


01:00:31.340 --> 01:00:32.858
as everybody else in the stands,


01:00:32.858 --> 01:00:35.017
that he rode away from the 360


01:00:35.017 --> 01:00:37.495
because he stuck in the side
of the landing,


01:00:37.495 --> 01:00:39.173
<i> he landed in the soft stuff
a little bit,</i>


01:00:39.173 --> 01:00:41.451
<i> and muscled it out.</i>


01:00:41.451 --> 01:00:42.610
<i> Brian Deegan has done</i>


01:00:42.610 --> 01:00:44.568
<i>the impossible on a dirt bike.</i>


01:00:44.568 --> 01:00:46.605
<i> The landing sketchy,
but he pulls it...</i>


01:00:46.605 --> 01:00:48.322
<i>Before I go off
to my final run,</i>


01:00:48.322 --> 01:00:50.401
Jim, my best friend comes in,


01:00:50.401 --> 01:00:52.440
he goes, "Deegan did a 360.


01:00:52.440 --> 01:00:54.398
It was the coolest
thing ever!"


01:00:54.398 --> 01:00:55.717
<i> "What?"</i>


01:00:55.717 --> 01:00:57.156
You're telling me
I'm risking my life


01:00:57.156 --> 01:00:59.513
to go out here
and do this trick


01:00:59.513 --> 01:01:01.031
<i> that I think is gonna set
the world on fire</i>


01:01:01.031 --> 01:01:02.869
<i> and Brian Deegan's
already done it?</i>


01:01:02.869 --> 01:01:03.989
<i> So, a trick that I invented</i>


01:01:03.989 --> 01:01:05.347
<i> and figured out how to do,</i>


01:01:05.347 --> 01:01:07.385
I now have to call
a "Mulisha Twist?"


01:01:07.385 --> 01:01:08.425
He was like, "Yup.


01:01:08.425 --> 01:01:10.382
It was awesome!"


01:01:10.382 --> 01:01:12.461
<i>People said backflips
would be impossible.</i>


01:01:12.461 --> 01:01:15.177
<i> 360s we thought
were way harder...</i>


01:01:15.177 --> 01:01:16.416
<i> Ridding up the peristyle</i>


01:01:16.416 --> 01:01:17.535
and Pastrana was up


01:01:17.535 --> 01:01:19.174
and he's like shaking his head


01:01:19.174 --> 01:01:20.213
<i> 'cause he knew</i>


01:01:20.213 --> 01:01:22.490
<i> he had to do that to win.</i>


01:01:22.490 --> 01:01:24.369
<i> 360, is it a 360 flip?</i>


01:01:24.369 --> 01:01:25.408
<i> What is it?</i>


01:01:25.408 --> 01:01:26.767
<i> It is just amazing.</i>


01:01:26.767 --> 01:01:28.605
<i> Ladies and gentlemen,</i>


01:01:28.605 --> 01:01:29.884
<i> I don't know
if anybody will pull</i>


01:01:29.884 --> 01:01:31.641
<i> anything like that</i>


01:01:31.641 --> 01:01:33.279
<i> any time soon
in freestyle motocross.</i>


01:01:33.279 --> 01:01:34.598
<i> I think--but we know that</i>


01:01:34.598 --> 01:01:35.677
<i> the 360 is possible.</i>


01:01:35.677 --> 01:01:36.916
<i> We know Travis Pastrana</i>


01:01:36.916 --> 01:01:38.275
<i> has been working on it.</i>


01:01:38.275 --> 01:01:39.793
<i> Will he throw it down?</i>


01:01:39.793 --> 01:01:41.512
<i> That is the question here.</i>


01:01:43.311 --> 01:01:45.069
He goes out.
He's stomping his run


01:01:45.069 --> 01:01:46.627
and he's hyping the crowd up,
and I'm like,


01:01:46.627 --> 01:01:48.306
"All right,
he's got to do the 360 now."


01:01:59.215 --> 01:02:00.574
<i> He comes around,</i>


01:02:00.574 --> 01:02:02.133
<i> same jump, same place,</i>


01:02:02.133 --> 01:02:04.011
<i> and Travis goes
and does the trick</i>


01:02:04.011 --> 01:02:05.849
<i>and he falls down and crashes.</i>


01:02:10.285 --> 01:02:11.643
<i> Oh!</i>


01:02:11.643 --> 01:02:12.722
<i> And he stands up</i>


01:02:12.722 --> 01:02:14.320
<i> and he's going one more.</i>


01:02:14.320 --> 01:02:15.679
<i> And I'm going,
"You don't get one more.</i>


01:02:15.679 --> 01:02:16.797
Time's running out."


01:02:16.797 --> 01:02:18.396
But I see he's calling time.


01:02:21.792 --> 01:02:22.831
<i>I just remember him going like,</i>


01:02:22.831 --> 01:02:24.230
"One more," to the crowd.


01:02:24.230 --> 01:02:25.668
Just, like, I don't know
what he was doing.


01:02:25.668 --> 01:02:26.787
In X Games rules


01:02:26.787 --> 01:02:28.306
you can call time out


01:02:28.306 --> 01:02:30.343
with any kind of
mechanical malfunction.


01:02:30.343 --> 01:02:33.063
So, of course,
my levers were bent.


01:02:33.063 --> 01:02:34.741
<i> So, I had to knock my levers
back straight.</i>


01:02:34.741 --> 01:02:36.499
<i> So, I got one more jump,</i>


01:02:36.499 --> 01:02:38.137
<i> according to the rules.</i>


01:02:38.137 --> 01:02:40.415
<i> Los Angeles</i>


01:02:42.693 --> 01:02:45.569
<i> He gonna do it
for one more time.</i>


01:03:06.668 --> 01:03:07.708
<i> I landed the trick.</i>


01:03:07.708 --> 01:03:09.147
<i> The crowd goes nuts.</i>


01:03:09.147 --> 01:03:10.984
<i> And, uh, you know,
I went out there,</i>


01:03:10.984 --> 01:03:12.623
ended up winning
the gold medal.


01:03:14.541 --> 01:03:15.980
And Deegan will never let me
live it down.


01:03:15.980 --> 01:03:17.019
Every time something happens,


01:03:17.019 --> 01:03:18.457
he's like, "Oh, time out, guys.


01:03:18.457 --> 01:03:19.616
Time out!"


01:03:19.616 --> 01:03:20.655
<i> We had a good battle</i>


01:03:20.655 --> 01:03:22.493
<i> and I walked away from there</i>


01:03:22.493 --> 01:03:23.853
<i> saying, "Hey, you know what?</i>


01:03:23.853 --> 01:03:25.651
<i> You landed the first 360
on dirt.</i>


01:03:25.651 --> 01:03:27.090
You set the bar."


01:03:27.090 --> 01:03:28.808
Like, that was it,
and that was a huge moment


01:03:28.808 --> 01:03:31.526
I'll never forget in my life.


01:03:31.526 --> 01:03:34.003
<i> As bitter as I wanted to be,</i>


01:03:34.003 --> 01:03:36.121
I was so proud


01:03:36.121 --> 01:03:37.560
of that crazy bastard


01:03:37.560 --> 01:03:39.119
because I knew how long


01:03:39.119 --> 01:03:40.877
<i> it took me to land
that stupid trick,</i>


01:03:40.877 --> 01:03:42.195
<i> and the fact that
he figured it out</i>


01:03:42.195 --> 01:03:43.514
before the X Games,


01:03:43.514 --> 01:03:45.552
is pretty damn cool.


01:03:45.552 --> 01:03:46.950
<i> No one could fathom it,</i>


01:03:46.950 --> 01:03:49.387
<i> but things were about
to get crazier.</i>


01:03:49.387 --> 01:03:51.984
<i> What came next was so insane,</i>


01:03:51.984 --> 01:03:53.543
<i> riders like Pastrana and Hart</i>


01:03:53.543 --> 01:03:54.942
<i> opted out entirely.</i>


01:03:54.942 --> 01:03:56.101
<i> Freestyle motocross</i>


01:03:56.101 --> 01:03:58.458
<i> was just so incredible</i>


01:03:58.458 --> 01:04:00.377
<i> and so popular</i>


01:04:00.377 --> 01:04:02.735
we got to have more of it.


01:04:02.735 --> 01:04:04.732
But what can we possibly
squeeze in there


01:04:04.732 --> 01:04:06.730
that we haven't already done?


01:04:06.730 --> 01:04:08.689
Well, wait,
we've got a second X Games


01:04:08.689 --> 01:04:09.768
every year,


01:04:09.768 --> 01:04:11.046
in the winter time.


01:04:11.046 --> 01:04:12.484
<i> The story is,</i>


01:04:12.484 --> 01:04:13.524
<i> who's gonna take home
gold today</i>


01:04:13.524 --> 01:04:14.844
<i> with a backflip variation?</i>


01:04:14.844 --> 01:04:15.883
<i> And, Jerry, right now</i>


01:04:15.883 --> 01:04:16.962
<i> the weather, so far so good,</i>


01:04:16.962 --> 01:04:18.360
<i> we've got some cloud cover</i>


01:04:18.360 --> 01:04:19.879
<i> that's making
for good visibility.</i>


01:04:19.879 --> 01:04:21.717
<i> We find these screws
that you can put</i>


01:04:21.717 --> 01:04:23.275
<i> in your dirt bike tires</i>


01:04:23.275 --> 01:04:24.315
<i> that are gonna
give you traction</i>


01:04:24.315 --> 01:04:27.031
<i> on ice or so we hear.</i>


01:04:29.150 --> 01:04:30.389
<i> We now have to create</i>


01:04:30.389 --> 01:04:32.266
this absolutely giant,


01:04:32.266 --> 01:04:33.785
giant landing


01:04:33.785 --> 01:04:35.262
because it's got to be
big enough


01:04:35.262 --> 01:04:36.342
for the guys to be able to


01:04:36.342 --> 01:04:38.100
jump up and land on to


01:04:38.100 --> 01:04:40.417
<i> and we need the room
for forgiveness.</i>


01:04:40.417 --> 01:04:41.776
If you're not scared,
you should be.


01:04:41.776 --> 01:04:43.735
Cam, look at this,
the snow deck landing.


01:04:43.735 --> 01:04:44.973
It stands about three stories


01:04:44.973 --> 01:04:46.372
above my head.


01:04:46.372 --> 01:04:47.531
<i> Riding Winter X was gnarly.</i>


01:04:47.531 --> 01:04:48.569
<i>A lot of people were just like,</i>


01:04:48.569 --> 01:04:50.247
"Oh, it's snow, you're fine."


01:04:50.247 --> 01:04:51.607
You know, "If you crash,
it's just snow."


01:04:51.607 --> 01:04:54.005
You're like, "No, it's ice


01:04:54.005 --> 01:04:55.083
that they've been
building this jump


01:04:55.083 --> 01:04:56.242
<i> for a month, and soaking it</i>


01:04:56.242 --> 01:04:57.560
<i>every day and every night with,</i>


01:04:57.560 --> 01:04:59.320
<i> hoses to make a block of ice,</i>


01:04:59.320 --> 01:05:00.758
<i> that's just as hard
as concrete."</i>


01:05:00.758 --> 01:05:02.157
<i>It's like a hundred-foot ice lip.</i>


01:05:02.157 --> 01:05:04.115
<i> A big 15 foot ice takeoff</i>


01:05:04.115 --> 01:05:05.795
<i> with a big ice landing</i>


01:05:05.795 --> 01:05:06.833
<i> and it's like,</i>


01:05:06.833 --> 01:05:08.272
"It's not powder, this is ice."


01:05:08.272 --> 01:05:09.590
<i> We put studs in our tires,</i>


01:05:09.590 --> 01:05:11.348
<i> and the snow breaks away,</i>


01:05:11.348 --> 01:05:13.027
and it forms ruts,
and it gets really,


01:05:13.027 --> 01:05:15.225
really crappy to jump.


01:05:15.225 --> 01:05:16.824
<i> use your...</i>


01:05:16.824 --> 01:05:18.421
<i> look for your landing.</i>


01:05:18.421 --> 01:05:19.780
These are desert rats.


01:05:19.780 --> 01:05:21.818
These guys aren't used
to being like,


01:05:21.818 --> 01:05:23.815
you know, all bundled up


01:05:23.815 --> 01:05:26.053
<i> because it's minus 10 degrees</i>


01:05:26.053 --> 01:05:28.212
<i> with their bike just, like,</i>


01:05:28.212 --> 01:05:29.650
<i> performing like crap</i>


01:05:29.650 --> 01:05:31.608
<i> because they're at
8,000 plus feet.</i>


01:05:31.608 --> 01:05:34.045
<i> So there were just
an insane amount</i>


01:05:34.045 --> 01:05:35.564
<i>of challenges that went against</i>


01:05:35.564 --> 01:05:36.883
<i> the event we're gonna do.</i>


01:05:36.883 --> 01:05:38.921
<i> Plus, it was a best trick.</i>


01:05:38.921 --> 01:05:40.919
So, we've taken
the most insane thing


01:05:40.919 --> 01:05:42.197
you could possibly do


01:05:42.197 --> 01:05:44.636
in the sport
of freestyle motocross


01:05:44.636 --> 01:05:47.513
and we put it on an ice block.


01:05:50.830 --> 01:05:52.028
<i> The direction,</i>


01:05:52.028 --> 01:05:53.826
the momentum,


01:05:53.826 --> 01:05:56.464
it wasn't anything
anybody had control over.


01:05:56.464 --> 01:05:57.983
<i> I remember flying to Winter X</i>


01:05:57.983 --> 01:06:00.061
<i> and I felt like
I had so much pressure on me</i>


01:06:00.061 --> 01:06:01.220
coming off the 360


01:06:01.220 --> 01:06:03.178
and one of the hardest things


01:06:03.178 --> 01:06:04.336
being a freestyler,


01:06:04.336 --> 01:06:06.056
or being a winner,
or being on top,


01:06:06.056 --> 01:06:07.294
you live with that pressure.


01:06:07.294 --> 01:06:08.412
<i> It's such a high expectation</i>


01:06:08.412 --> 01:06:09.651
<i> to live up to every event</i>


01:06:09.651 --> 01:06:11.010
<i> and then coming to Winter X,</i>


01:06:11.010 --> 01:06:12.329
<i> I just felt like,
"I have to win again.</i>


01:06:12.329 --> 01:06:13.648
I have to win and."


01:06:13.648 --> 01:06:15.605
I was like, "Oh, Deegan
is winning X Games for sure.


01:06:15.605 --> 01:06:17.323
He's doing the 360
on the 95 foot jump."


01:06:17.323 --> 01:06:19.042
<i> Brian Deegan understands</i>


01:06:19.042 --> 01:06:21.440
<i> that if he's going to win
this competition,</i>


01:06:21.440 --> 01:06:22.958
<i> and if he's going to meet
the expectation</i>


01:06:22.958 --> 01:06:25.955
<i> of the adoring hordes
of Mulisha fans,</i>


01:06:25.955 --> 01:06:27.434
<i> he has to pull
the Mulisha Twist.</i>


01:06:27.434 --> 01:06:29.631
He's got to do this big 360.


01:06:29.631 --> 01:06:31.390
<i>I've lined up and
you see, you know, when I look,</i>


01:06:31.390 --> 01:06:32.469
<i> crowd on each side,
thousands of people.</i>


01:06:32.469 --> 01:06:33.587
Cameras there,
ambulance there.


01:06:33.587 --> 01:06:34.628
Here we go again.


01:06:34.628 --> 01:06:36.225
You know, amazing.


01:06:53.967 --> 01:06:55.486
You're in the air in a jump,


01:06:55.486 --> 01:06:57.005
it seems like,
"Oh, it's just a few seconds."


01:06:57.005 --> 01:06:58.324
<i>But, when you are in mid-flight</i>


01:06:58.324 --> 01:06:59.803
<i> and it's going wrong,</i>


01:06:59.803 --> 01:07:02.160
<i> it seems like an eternity.</i>


01:07:06.756 --> 01:07:08.554
<i>Instantly, shatters both arms.</i>


01:07:08.554 --> 01:07:09.593
<i> Land on my hip,</i>


01:07:09.593 --> 01:07:10.632
<i> shatters my femur,</i>


01:07:10.632 --> 01:07:12.470
<i> and five spots on my hip.</i>


01:07:12.470 --> 01:07:13.949
When they say
unbearable pain,


01:07:13.949 --> 01:07:15.547
like, that's what it was,
it was like


01:07:15.547 --> 01:07:17.265
<i> I couldn't even
handle the pain.</i>


01:07:17.265 --> 01:07:18.865
<i> And now I'm starting
to have internal bleeding</i>


01:07:18.865 --> 01:07:20.582
<i> and, you know,
I was just laying there like</i>


01:07:20.582 --> 01:07:22.181
"Oh, my God!"
I remember I tried to get up


01:07:22.181 --> 01:07:23.938
and my arms are bent backwards


01:07:23.938 --> 01:07:26.337
<i> and I'm just laying there,
I'm like,</i>


01:07:26.337 --> 01:07:27.376
<i> "Oh, man, I'm fucked!"</i>


01:07:33.450 --> 01:07:34.929
<i> Visiting Brian in hospital</i>


01:07:34.929 --> 01:07:37.127
<i> the week after his crash
in Aspen,</i>


01:07:37.127 --> 01:07:38.166
<i> I mean, literally,</i>


01:07:38.166 --> 01:07:39.403
<i> he can't do anything.</i>


01:07:39.403 --> 01:07:42.002
He's completely broken.


01:07:42.002 --> 01:07:43.040
<i> It was around the clock</i>


01:07:43.040 --> 01:07:44.199
<i> taking care of him.</i>


01:07:44.199 --> 01:07:45.517
<i> Having to hold that
pee cup for him</i>


01:07:45.517 --> 01:07:46.557
<i> to go to the bathroom</i>


01:07:46.557 --> 01:07:47.836
<i> all throughout the night,</i>


01:07:47.836 --> 01:07:49.474
<i> giving pain medication,</i>


01:07:49.474 --> 01:07:51.432
Seran wrapping him with plastic


01:07:51.432 --> 01:07:53.151
and having to sit him
in the shower,


01:07:53.151 --> 01:07:55.389
I'd have to fully bathe him.


01:07:55.389 --> 01:07:56.868
<i> I sat there thinking
like, "Dude,</i>


01:07:56.868 --> 01:07:58.546
<i> what are you doing here?"
You know, like,</i>


01:07:58.546 --> 01:07:59.864
"You could be doing
something else.


01:07:59.864 --> 01:08:01.582
Why are you doing this?"
You know, all that


01:08:01.582 --> 01:08:02.622
just went through my head.


01:08:02.622 --> 01:08:04.540
I crashed on Saturday,


01:08:04.540 --> 01:08:06.257
last--has it even been--


01:08:07.456 --> 01:08:09.935
you know, it's five days


01:08:09.935 --> 01:08:13.011
I'm already up walking around.


01:08:13.011 --> 01:08:14.050
Cruising around just went


01:08:14.050 --> 01:08:16.928
and had my second turd


01:08:16.928 --> 01:08:19.126
which is a pretty


01:08:19.126 --> 01:08:20.644
good accomplishment


01:08:20.644 --> 01:08:23.002
for being on
all these pain meds.


01:08:23.002 --> 01:08:24.680
<i> It was bad,
that hospital trip is--</i>


01:08:24.680 --> 01:08:26.038
was the worse.


01:08:26.038 --> 01:08:27.318
We expect your victory


01:08:27.318 --> 01:08:28.356
and that your gold medal


01:08:28.356 --> 01:08:31.154
to be dedicated to this team


01:08:31.154 --> 01:08:32.593
next year, for sure.


01:08:32.593 --> 01:08:34.191
That's the least I could do.


01:08:34.191 --> 01:08:36.309
I'm sure, if I'm back
winning by next year.


01:08:36.309 --> 01:08:37.547
<i> It's a long road.</i>


01:08:37.547 --> 01:08:39.866
<i> It's not pretty, it's hard.</i>


01:08:39.866 --> 01:08:42.183
And to the person
watching on TV,


01:08:42.183 --> 01:08:43.421
to the person up
in the stands,


01:08:43.421 --> 01:08:44.660
"Wow, that was cool!"


01:08:44.660 --> 01:08:46.619
You know,
but what they don't see


01:08:46.619 --> 01:08:49.096
is what goes on
behind the scenes.


01:08:49.096 --> 01:08:50.455
It's good to get outside.


01:08:50.455 --> 01:08:52.333
Oh, not bad.


01:08:52.333 --> 01:08:54.132
<i>We know what the consequences are.</i>


01:08:54.132 --> 01:08:55.570
<i> For whatever fear you have</i>


01:08:55.570 --> 01:08:57.088
<i> that caused that fear
in your head.</i>


01:08:57.088 --> 01:08:57.608
<i> Hey, buddy.</i>


01:08:57.608 --> 01:09:00.165
You know you got to go
out there and do it again.


01:09:00.165 --> 01:09:01.485
I figured I have experienced
the most pain


01:09:01.485 --> 01:09:02.963
I've ever experienced, so,


01:09:02.963 --> 01:09:04.961
<i> there's not really a lot
more to fear.</i>


01:09:04.961 --> 01:09:06.280
They're able to just go on


01:09:06.280 --> 01:09:07.558
with their daily routines,


01:09:07.558 --> 01:09:09.956
<i> train in pain,</i>


01:09:09.956 --> 01:09:12.113
<i> perform in pain,
and they just do it.</i>


01:09:12.113 --> 01:09:13.391
And they don't complain
about it.


01:09:13.391 --> 01:09:15.229
<i>Humans have an amazing ability</i>


01:09:15.229 --> 01:09:16.748
<i> to forget bad things.</i>


01:09:16.748 --> 01:09:18.149
<i> And I think
that's what happens</i>


01:09:18.149 --> 01:09:19.187
to these guys.


01:09:19.187 --> 01:09:20.945
They--they're injured,


01:09:20.945 --> 01:09:22.663
<i> but they love
the thrill of doing it,</i>


01:09:22.663 --> 01:09:24.422
<i> and then after
the pain subsides,</i>


01:09:24.422 --> 01:09:25.781
<i> or after they go through</i>


01:09:25.781 --> 01:09:27.299
<i> a certain amount
of recuperation,</i>


01:09:27.299 --> 01:09:29.297
<i> they almost forget about it.</i>


01:09:29.297 --> 01:09:32.535
I broke 17 ribs,


01:09:32.535 --> 01:09:35.930
punctured my lungs 3 times,


01:09:35.930 --> 01:09:38.568
broke 9 vertebras in my back,


01:09:38.568 --> 01:09:40.047
lacerated my liver,


01:09:40.047 --> 01:09:41.925
smashed my right kidney,
which is gone,


01:09:41.925 --> 01:09:43.923
broke my face,


01:09:43.923 --> 01:09:45.842
collar bone shoulder,
shoulder blade,


01:09:45.842 --> 01:09:47.520
hematomas on both hips.


01:09:47.520 --> 01:09:48.918
<i> Seeing Mike ride</i>


01:09:48.918 --> 01:09:50.397
<i> and just knowing that like</i>


01:09:50.397 --> 01:09:51.755
<i> that's where he is free,</i>


01:09:51.755 --> 01:09:53.793
<i> you know, that's who he is,</i>


01:09:53.793 --> 01:09:54.833
<i> that's what he is,</i>


01:09:54.833 --> 01:09:57.029
<i> that's the love of his life.</i>


01:09:57.029 --> 01:09:58.308
You can't take that
away from him.


01:09:58.308 --> 01:09:59.667
<i> The doctor did tell Brian</i>


01:09:59.667 --> 01:10:01.105
<i> don't get back
on a dirt bike again,</i>


01:10:01.105 --> 01:10:03.263
like never again.
The doctor told him "No."


01:10:03.263 --> 01:10:05.461
We get home and the second
he can get back up


01:10:05.461 --> 01:10:07.140
on that bike
he's on there, quick.


01:10:07.140 --> 01:10:09.618
<i> Well, it's not just about
the broken bones</i>


01:10:09.618 --> 01:10:11.017
<i> and...</i>


01:10:11.017 --> 01:10:14.093
you know, the chance
of being paralyzed or,


01:10:14.093 --> 01:10:16.292
you know losing a contract,


01:10:16.292 --> 01:10:17.650
and not being able to pay
your bills.


01:10:17.650 --> 01:10:21.047
This is a lot more serious.


01:10:21.047 --> 01:10:22.886
You could lose your life.


01:10:22.886 --> 01:10:24.603
I could lose my husband,


01:10:24.603 --> 01:10:27.161
my kids could not
have their dad


01:10:27.161 --> 01:10:29.599
at any minute.


01:10:29.599 --> 01:10:31.077
<i>You have to be able to decide.</i>


01:10:31.077 --> 01:10:32.716
<i> When I go up the takeoff
of this ramp,</i>


01:10:32.716 --> 01:10:34.314
that bone that's sticking
through the skin,


01:10:34.314 --> 01:10:35.952
"Can we duct tape that
and will it hold?"


01:10:35.952 --> 01:10:37.232
<i> And it's a matter of how much</i>


01:10:37.232 --> 01:10:38.670
<i> you're willing
to deal with.</i>


01:10:38.670 --> 01:10:40.308
And that's why I like
freestyle so much,


01:10:40.308 --> 01:10:41.467
<i> it was because</i>


01:10:41.467 --> 01:10:43.464
<i> it was a shorter duration.</i>


01:10:43.464 --> 01:10:44.663
<i> You had the adrenaline,</i>


01:10:44.663 --> 01:10:46.421
<i> you had, you know, the crowd,</i>


01:10:46.421 --> 01:10:48.339
<i> you had the--everything
that fired you up.</i>


01:10:48.339 --> 01:10:50.017
And you could overcome


01:10:50.017 --> 01:10:52.017
insurmountable pain


01:10:52.017 --> 01:10:53.774
for a very short
duration of time,


01:10:53.774 --> 01:10:55.453
and still be successful
in what you do.


01:10:57.730 --> 01:10:59.250
<i> Well, Sal,
to be honest with you,</i>


01:10:59.250 --> 01:11:00.688
<i> I think it's a better
Brian Deegan.</i>


01:11:00.688 --> 01:11:01.767
<i> He has taken the injury</i>


01:11:01.767 --> 01:11:03.326
<i> and started working harder.</i>


01:11:03.326 --> 01:11:04.485
<i> The training and the rise...</i>


01:11:04.485 --> 01:11:05.523
<i> A year later,</i>


01:11:05.523 --> 01:11:07.162
<i> he's back in Aspen,</i>


01:11:07.162 --> 01:11:09.320
on his bike,


01:11:09.320 --> 01:11:11.678
<i> at this, you know,
huge ice-cube again.</i>


01:11:11.678 --> 01:11:13.197
<i> Think of all the things</i>


01:11:13.197 --> 01:11:14.875
<i> going through
Brian's head right now.</i>


01:11:14.875 --> 01:11:16.074
<i>Well, Brian, obviously,
suffered last year.</i>


01:11:16.074 --> 01:11:17.592
<i> He called us every week</i>


01:11:17.592 --> 01:11:19.510
<i> talking about
the build of this course.</i>


01:11:19.510 --> 01:11:20.949
<i> He was very concerned</i>


01:11:20.949 --> 01:11:22.507
<i> that we get some
of the ramps smaller</i>


01:11:22.507 --> 01:11:24.066
<i> and more consistent
than last year...</i>


01:11:24.066 --> 01:11:25.585
<i> I was nervous the whole time.</i>


01:11:25.585 --> 01:11:27.342
<i> I couldn't get out
of the zone.</i>


01:11:27.342 --> 01:11:28.421
You know, I was like


01:11:28.421 --> 01:11:29.660
"Man, hopefully I--you know,


01:11:29.660 --> 01:11:31.098
I don't want
to get hurt again."


01:11:31.098 --> 01:11:32.336
<i> And all those thoughts.</i>


01:11:32.336 --> 01:11:33.535
<i> Brian Deegan is coming up,</i>


01:11:33.535 --> 01:11:36.094
<i> he's facing the monster.</i>


01:11:38.411 --> 01:11:39.809
<i> Brian's waiting.</i>


01:11:39.809 --> 01:11:40.848
<i> It's cold.</i>


01:11:40.848 --> 01:11:42.047
<i> The pressure's on.</i>


01:11:43.526 --> 01:11:45.404
You're facing down
that demon.


01:11:45.404 --> 01:11:48.281
You're staring him
straight in the eyes.


01:11:49.922 --> 01:11:51.679
<i> And you know what happens</i>


01:11:51.679 --> 01:11:53.077
<i> when it goes wrong.</i>


01:11:56.194 --> 01:11:57.234
<i>Ladies and gentlemen,
will it be</i>


01:11:57.234 --> 01:11:58.393
<i> a backflip variation?</i>


01:11:58.393 --> 01:11:59.752
<i> Will it be a 360?</i>


01:11:59.752 --> 01:12:01.430
<i> Now is a good time
to stand up.</i>


01:12:01.430 --> 01:12:02.748
<i>I'm like,
"You just got to lay down</i>


01:12:02.748 --> 01:12:04.346
<i> one good trick just do it.</i>


01:12:04.346 --> 01:12:05.386
<i> If you crash or whatever,</i>


01:12:05.386 --> 01:12:06.665
<i> just block it out."</i>


01:12:06.665 --> 01:12:07.943
You know, "Just do it,
you're here."


01:12:07.943 --> 01:12:09.661
And I remember
the same exact feeling


01:12:09.661 --> 01:12:10.700
as I took off.


01:12:25.125 --> 01:12:26.164
I pulled the flip trick off


01:12:26.164 --> 01:12:27.763
and won X Games,


01:12:27.763 --> 01:12:28.842
<i> and I was like, "You did it.</i>


01:12:28.842 --> 01:12:29.921
<i> All right, dude. It's done."</i>


01:12:29.921 --> 01:12:31.199
<i> And it was such
a sigh of relief</i>


01:12:31.199 --> 01:12:32.678
<i> and such a different feeling,</i>


01:12:32.678 --> 01:12:34.357
<i> you just accomplish it
and you got through it.</i>


01:12:34.357 --> 01:12:36.315
<i>Brian Deegan absolutely deserved</i>


01:12:36.315 --> 01:12:38.113
<i> every bit of stardom</i>


01:12:38.113 --> 01:12:40.152
<i> and accolade that he got,</i>


01:12:40.152 --> 01:12:41.671
because he put himself


01:12:41.671 --> 01:12:43.349
in harm's way again


01:12:43.349 --> 01:12:44.388
and again,


01:12:44.388 --> 01:12:45.746
and every time he went down


01:12:45.746 --> 01:12:47.065
he got back up


01:12:47.065 --> 01:12:48.144
<i> and went for it</i>


01:12:48.144 --> 01:12:50.142
<i> to prove that he was worthy</i>


01:12:50.142 --> 01:12:51.261
<i> of that spot.</i>


01:12:51.261 --> 01:12:52.300
<i> The dude comes back</i>


01:12:52.300 --> 01:12:53.659
<i> and wins the gold medal.</i>


01:12:53.659 --> 01:12:55.097
<i> And, you know again,</i>


01:12:55.097 --> 01:12:57.256
there's a great story to that,


01:12:57.256 --> 01:12:58.934
but it's, sort of, like,
"You know what?


01:12:58.934 --> 01:13:00.891
This is just being pushed


01:13:00.891 --> 01:13:02.569
a little too much."


01:13:02.569 --> 01:13:04.168
<i> Not long after,</i>


01:13:04.168 --> 01:13:05.966
<i> X Games would remove
freestyle best trick</i>


01:13:05.966 --> 01:13:07.884
<i> from winter competition.</i>


01:13:07.884 --> 01:13:09.003
<i> Still, on dirt,</i>


01:13:09.003 --> 01:13:10.122
<i> a new breed of athletes</i>


01:13:10.122 --> 01:13:11.601
<i>continued to push progression,</i>


01:13:11.601 --> 01:13:13.559
<i> with Nate Adams
leading the way.</i>


01:13:13.559 --> 01:13:15.117
<i> And new faces emerging,</i>


01:13:15.117 --> 01:13:17.674
<i> adding complex variations
to the backflip.</i>


01:13:17.674 --> 01:13:18.913
I think our sports,


01:13:18.913 --> 01:13:20.552
and freestyle motocross
in particular,


01:13:20.552 --> 01:13:22.550
it's just about--
it's about pushing limits.


01:13:22.550 --> 01:13:24.308
Pushing your own limits,
pushing the boundaries


01:13:24.308 --> 01:13:26.027
of what people think
is possible,


01:13:26.027 --> 01:13:29.864
and not caring what
anyone thinks in the process.


01:13:29.864 --> 01:13:31.901
<i> At the forefront
of this new progression,</i>


01:13:31.901 --> 01:13:34.020
<i> Travis Pastrana
contemplated a trick</i>


01:13:34.020 --> 01:13:37.016
<i> that most riders believed
was truly impossible.</i>


01:13:39.614 --> 01:13:42.332
<i> Since we introduced
best trick to X Games,</i>


01:13:42.332 --> 01:13:44.689
<i> it completely changed
the whole playing field,</i>


01:13:44.689 --> 01:13:46.646
because you needed
to come into X Games


01:13:46.646 --> 01:13:49.684
every year with something new.


01:13:49.684 --> 01:13:51.042
<i> I heard the rumors
and I was like,</i>


01:13:51.042 --> 01:13:52.401
"Yeah, right.
He's gonna try that,"


01:13:52.401 --> 01:13:53.599
and, you know, whatever.


01:13:53.599 --> 01:13:55.358
<i> I think, once an athlete,</i>


01:13:55.358 --> 01:13:57.636
<i> especially an action
sports athlete,</i>


01:13:57.636 --> 01:13:59.874
comes up with
this crazy scenario


01:13:59.874 --> 01:14:03.311
<i> in the back of their skull,
it's on.</i>


01:14:03.311 --> 01:14:05.828
The idea of someone
doing a double backflip


01:14:05.828 --> 01:14:08.105
on a 200 and something-pound
motorcycle


01:14:08.105 --> 01:14:10.703
is--it's on
the verge of lunacy.


01:14:10.703 --> 01:14:12.261
<i>It's pretty simple,
though, to understand</i>


01:14:12.261 --> 01:14:14.779
<i> if you don't pull
the double backflip,</i>


01:14:14.779 --> 01:14:17.617
what part of the rotation
are you in when you land?


01:14:17.617 --> 01:14:20.694
You know, it's in a--
it's a bad place to be.


01:14:20.694 --> 01:14:23.171
<i>He says he has a tendency
to over rotate it.</i>


01:14:23.171 --> 01:14:25.171
<i> He's gonna try
to go a little short.</i>


01:14:25.171 --> 01:14:26.609
Before he does his event,


01:14:26.609 --> 01:14:28.527
I always go to him,
give him a hug and kiss,


01:14:28.527 --> 01:14:29.685
"I love you,


01:14:29.685 --> 01:14:32.842
be safe, have fun,
good luck."


01:14:32.842 --> 01:14:35.399
We, kind of, say goodbye
without saying goodbye.


01:14:35.399 --> 01:14:36.957
<i> And then I leave,</i>


01:14:36.957 --> 01:14:39.915
<i> because I don't want
my stress on him.</i>


01:14:45.509 --> 01:14:48.267
<i>Once again, there's this incredible</i>


01:14:48.267 --> 01:14:50.465
sense of foreboding.


01:14:50.465 --> 01:14:52.302
<i>He is looking somber,</i>


01:14:52.302 --> 01:14:53.343
<i> he is looking scared.</i>


01:14:53.343 --> 01:14:54.741
<i> I had never seen him</i>


01:14:54.741 --> 01:14:56.778
with his head down,
and his body slouched,


01:14:56.778 --> 01:14:59.336
and the energy seemed to be
drained out of him.


01:14:59.336 --> 01:15:01.654
<i>I would get off the couch.</i>


01:15:01.654 --> 01:15:04.451
<i> Every rider in the house
is watching,</i>


01:15:04.451 --> 01:15:06.050
<i> the world is watching!</i>


01:15:06.050 --> 01:15:07.527
<i>It's pure electricity.</i>


01:15:07.527 --> 01:15:09.407
You know some people
got their eyes closed.


01:15:09.407 --> 01:15:12.045
<i> Some people probably
aren't even breathing.</i>


01:15:12.045 --> 01:15:14.002
Everybody literally held
a collective breath.


01:15:14.002 --> 01:15:15.201
And you could just


01:15:15.201 --> 01:15:17.799
the whole place at once
had paused.


01:15:19.237 --> 01:15:21.074
<i> "Oh, my God.</i>


01:15:21.074 --> 01:15:22.114
This is it."


01:15:22.114 --> 01:15:24.911
You know, I might never see


01:15:24.911 --> 01:15:25.870
my son again.


01:15:41.255 --> 01:15:42.694
<i> It's gonna work.</i>


01:15:42.694 --> 01:15:43.933
I'm like, "It's gonna work.


01:15:43.933 --> 01:15:45.691
<i> It's gonna work."</i>


01:15:50.007 --> 01:15:51.365
<i> And I saw the landing,</i>


01:15:51.365 --> 01:15:53.004
<i>and when you spot the landing,</i>


01:15:53.004 --> 01:15:54.682
<i> it slows down your rotation</i>


01:15:54.682 --> 01:15:55.961
<i>and I remember the motorcycle,
kind of, stopped.</i>


01:15:55.961 --> 01:15:57.959
And I thought
"I just killed myself."


01:16:04.352 --> 01:16:06.231
"Holy shit. It worked!"


01:16:22.056 --> 01:16:24.214
<i> A double backflip</i>


01:16:24.214 --> 01:16:27.211
<i> from Travis Pastrana.</i>


01:16:27.211 --> 01:16:28.808
<i> When I landed that double flip,</i>


01:16:28.808 --> 01:16:30.008
<i> and I was riding away,</i>


01:16:30.008 --> 01:16:32.126
and everybody in the stadium


01:16:32.126 --> 01:16:33.764
felt what I felt,


01:16:33.764 --> 01:16:34.883
that's something
that not many athletes


01:16:34.883 --> 01:16:36.282
will ever get to experience.


01:16:40.758 --> 01:16:42.316
I'm sorry, mom.


01:16:42.316 --> 01:16:44.274
Thank you for supporting me.


01:16:44.274 --> 01:16:45.593
<i> People afterwards said,</i>


01:16:45.593 --> 01:16:47.431
<i> "Why did he say
he was sorry?"</i>


01:16:47.431 --> 01:16:50.067
And I said "He didn't say
he's sorry that he did it.


01:16:50.067 --> 01:16:52.866
He was sorry that
he put me through that."


01:16:52.866 --> 01:16:54.464
And I understood that.


01:16:54.464 --> 01:16:56.022
You know, I understood that.


01:16:58.701 --> 01:17:00.419
I actually feel
really bad for my mom


01:17:00.419 --> 01:17:02.097
<i> because she wants
the best for me.</i>


01:17:02.097 --> 01:17:03.575
<i> She wants me
to chase my dreams,</i>


01:17:03.575 --> 01:17:05.013
<i> she wants to support me
chasing my dreams,</i>


01:17:05.013 --> 01:17:07.013
<i> she wants to help me
chase my dreams,</i>


01:17:07.013 --> 01:17:08.490
but she doesn't wanna
see me get hurt,


01:17:08.490 --> 01:17:10.968
and in these sports,


01:17:10.968 --> 01:17:12.206
you can't have both.


01:17:14.405 --> 01:17:16.922
<i> Watching Travis Pastrana
do a double backflip</i>


01:17:16.922 --> 01:17:18.241
at X Games,


01:17:18.241 --> 01:17:21.318
was by far the most
breathtaking feat


01:17:21.318 --> 01:17:23.436
I've seen anybody ever do in--


01:17:23.436 --> 01:17:26.033
with any sport
in the history of mankind.


01:17:26.033 --> 01:17:27.912
<i> You can put them
in these parameters</i>


01:17:27.912 --> 01:17:30.230
<i> and people think,
"This is all you can do."</i>


01:17:30.230 --> 01:17:32.387
But then, for a guy
like Travis Pastrana,


01:17:32.387 --> 01:17:35.465
thinks of something
totally outside the box,


01:17:35.465 --> 01:17:36.863
and makes everybody scratch
a hole in their head,


01:17:36.863 --> 01:17:38.620
going, "Where does it stop?"


01:17:57.124 --> 01:17:58.762
<i>This is his shot.</i>


01:17:58.762 --> 01:18:01.599
<i> This could launch
his whole career right here.</i>


01:18:01.599 --> 01:18:03.118
<i> When the second generation</i>


01:18:03.118 --> 01:18:05.076
<i> of freestyle riders
arrived at the X Games,</i>


01:18:05.076 --> 01:18:07.513
<i> the bar was already
impossibly high.</i>


01:18:07.513 --> 01:18:08.632
<i> For Brian Deegan,</i>


01:18:08.632 --> 01:18:09.951
<i>it was time to put his personal</i>


01:18:09.951 --> 01:18:11.710
<i> competitive goals aside</i>


01:18:11.710 --> 01:18:13.747
<i> and take a rising star
under his wing.</i>


01:18:13.747 --> 01:18:15.706
<i> Brian definitely felt Jeremy,</i>


01:18:15.706 --> 01:18:17.063
being younger than him,


01:18:17.063 --> 01:18:19.183
was like the next generation
to come up.


01:18:19.183 --> 01:18:21.221
<i> He wanted to help him
create that path</i>


01:18:21.221 --> 01:18:22.658
<i> and make that way.</i>


01:18:22.658 --> 01:18:24.296
<i> We rode together every day.</i>


01:18:24.296 --> 01:18:26.934
<i> I pushed him in his normal
everyday business life,</i>


01:18:26.934 --> 01:18:28.452
and I could trust him.


01:18:30.010 --> 01:18:31.968
<i> He goes to the X Games</i>


01:18:31.968 --> 01:18:33.848
<i> and he just starts
laying it down.</i>


01:18:33.848 --> 01:18:35.406
<i>Underflip.</i>


01:18:35.406 --> 01:18:37.764
The tricks that he had
were stunning.


01:18:37.764 --> 01:18:39.562
<i> Flip and knack,
getting it over</i>


01:18:39.562 --> 01:18:40.920
<i>to the other side of the bike.</i>


01:18:40.920 --> 01:18:42.240
<i> The world was just like,</i>


01:18:42.240 --> 01:18:45.077
"Holy crap, Jeremy Lusk
is the guy!"


01:18:45.077 --> 01:18:47.394
<i>- Oh, for Lusk.
- Oh, he did it!</i>


01:18:47.394 --> 01:18:48.713
<i>Ninety-two point four zero!</i>


01:18:48.713 --> 01:18:49.873
<i> This dude just won X Games</i>


01:18:49.873 --> 01:18:51.511
like his second time there.


01:18:51.511 --> 01:18:53.388
<i>Jeremy Lusk just added his name</i>


01:18:53.388 --> 01:18:55.186
<i> alongside of Mike Metzger,</i>


01:18:55.186 --> 01:18:57.585
<i> Travis Pastrana,
and Nate Adams and Adam Jones</i>


01:18:57.585 --> 01:18:59.622
<i> as the only people
to ever get gold</i>


01:18:59.622 --> 01:19:01.341
<i> in Freestyle Moto X.</i>


01:19:01.341 --> 01:19:03.019
<i>The biggest payback
I could ever ask for,</i>


01:19:03.019 --> 01:19:04.738
<i> when you give
someone's opportunity,</i>


01:19:04.738 --> 01:19:05.657
<i> you help them with something</i>


01:19:05.657 --> 01:19:06.656
<i> and they pay you back</i>


01:19:06.656 --> 01:19:08.413
with the achievement of winning,


01:19:08.413 --> 01:19:09.732
that's the ultimate.


01:19:09.732 --> 01:19:11.451
And he, you know,
came into the sport,


01:19:11.451 --> 01:19:13.688
he was motivated,
he was dedicated,


01:19:13.688 --> 01:19:15.407
<i> he went from just
being this nobody</i>


01:19:15.407 --> 01:19:17.484
<i> to being on the top
of the sport in two years.</i>


01:19:17.484 --> 01:19:19.963
<i> It's like, He won X Games,
he won Rider of The Year,</i>


01:19:19.963 --> 01:19:22.480
<i> he married
his high school sweetheart,</i>


01:19:22.480 --> 01:19:24.438
I'm like, "Dude,
you're in a rush, aren't you?"


01:19:24.438 --> 01:19:26.437
He just couldn't get everything
done quick enough.


01:19:30.233 --> 01:19:32.431
<i> He's down in Costa Rica riding,</i>


01:19:32.431 --> 01:19:34.509
and someone called me
and left a message saying,


01:19:34.509 --> 01:19:36.307
"Hey, you need
to check on Lusk,


01:19:36.307 --> 01:19:37.306
he's at the hospital."


01:19:37.306 --> 01:19:39.464
I'm like, "Whoa, really?"


01:19:39.464 --> 01:19:40.863
In my head, he's tough.


01:19:40.863 --> 01:19:42.941
I've seen this dude
crash many times.


01:19:42.941 --> 01:19:45.259
<i> And so, I'm calling
the doctors,</i>


01:19:45.259 --> 01:19:47.696
<i> the promoter, the promoter
is acting really weird,</i>


01:19:47.696 --> 01:19:49.534
<i> like, I'm like,
"Hey, give me some answers!"</i>


01:19:49.534 --> 01:19:51.373
<i> He's like,
"Well, he's in the hospital."</i>


01:19:51.373 --> 01:19:53.729
<i> I couldn't really understand
his English too well.</i>


01:19:53.729 --> 01:19:55.607
You get like, kind of,
a scattered report.


01:19:55.607 --> 01:19:58.285
You're not really sure
what's going on


01:19:58.285 --> 01:19:59.723
but it was real serious.


01:19:59.723 --> 01:20:02.042
I felt like I needed
to go there.


01:20:02.042 --> 01:20:05.078
<i> We head out to Costa Rica.</i>


01:20:05.078 --> 01:20:07.715
<i> And we've land and we went
straight to the hospital.</i>


01:20:07.715 --> 01:20:09.315
<i> Walking down these
hallways there's like,</i>


01:20:09.315 --> 01:20:12.232
you hear people moaning
and that was just like,


01:20:12.232 --> 01:20:13.989
just third world.
And then, I said,


01:20:13.989 --> 01:20:15.429
<i> "Where's the doctor?
Where's the surgeon?"</i>


01:20:15.429 --> 01:20:16.428
<i> I'm like,
"What's gonna happen?"</i>


01:20:16.428 --> 01:20:17.468
<i> He's like, "Oh, he's not--</i>


01:20:17.468 --> 01:20:18.986
<i> probably not gonna make it."</i>


01:20:18.986 --> 01:20:20.544
Like--I was like,
"No way, we have to save him!"


01:20:20.544 --> 01:20:22.382
You know, and I start
calling around


01:20:22.382 --> 01:20:23.741
and saying "A life flight.


01:20:23.741 --> 01:20:24.780
We got to life
flight him home.


01:20:24.780 --> 01:20:26.139
Like, this place is a nightmare,


01:20:26.139 --> 01:20:27.418
like, there's no way
these doctors


01:20:27.418 --> 01:20:28.616
are doing the right thing."


01:20:28.616 --> 01:20:29.775
And they wouldn't do it.


01:20:29.775 --> 01:20:30.774
They're like "He's unstable.


01:20:30.774 --> 01:20:32.613
You can't take him."


01:20:32.613 --> 01:20:35.290
His dad just watched him
basically, pass away.


01:20:35.290 --> 01:20:38.727
And I was,
"There's nothing I could do."


01:20:38.727 --> 01:20:41.043
I mean, it's just really--


01:20:41.043 --> 01:20:44.919
he's, you know,
he's my best friend, so...


01:20:48.636 --> 01:20:51.033
You never wanna
believe it can happen


01:20:51.033 --> 01:20:53.911
and, unfortunately,
it happened, you know,


01:20:53.911 --> 01:20:56.229
and he's not here


01:20:56.229 --> 01:20:57.587
and all we could do


01:20:57.587 --> 01:20:59.385
is remember how great he was.


01:21:01.783 --> 01:21:03.461
<i> Finding out</i>


01:21:03.461 --> 01:21:05.980
<i> that he had lost his life,</i>


01:21:05.980 --> 01:21:08.498
actually competing in a--


01:21:08.498 --> 01:21:10.616
in a freestyle event,


01:21:10.616 --> 01:21:12.894
<i> was just--it was just weird,</i>


01:21:12.894 --> 01:21:15.851
<i> like, horrible wakeup call
for everybody.</i>


01:21:15.851 --> 01:21:19.807
<i> We've all known
how gnarly it's gotten to be,</i>


01:21:19.807 --> 01:21:21.245
it finally bit somebody.


01:21:21.245 --> 01:21:23.723
<i>And I think reality did set in</i>


01:21:23.723 --> 01:21:24.802
<i> in a harsh way.</i>


01:21:24.802 --> 01:21:26.879
<i> I know emotionally,</i>


01:21:26.879 --> 01:21:29.036
<i> it tore a lot of riders up.</i>


01:21:29.036 --> 01:21:30.236
To have someone actually die


01:21:30.236 --> 01:21:31.794
riding freestyle motocross


01:21:31.794 --> 01:21:34.151
it just really hit close
to home with all of us.


01:21:34.151 --> 01:21:36.469
Is it worth it?


01:21:36.469 --> 01:21:38.108
You know, would it
make more sense


01:21:38.108 --> 01:21:41.025
to just go
and get a regular job,


01:21:41.025 --> 01:21:42.663
and not have
to worry about this?


01:21:42.663 --> 01:21:44.822
<i> It put a cloud
over the sport.</i>


01:21:44.822 --> 01:21:47.019
<i>It made the young guys question
what they should be doing.</i>


01:21:47.019 --> 01:21:49.457
It made the old guys question
should they still be doing it?


01:21:49.457 --> 01:21:51.774
<i> I never thought
that throughout my whole career</i>


01:21:51.774 --> 01:21:53.333
<i> until Lusk died
riding his dirt bike</i>


01:21:53.333 --> 01:21:56.131
that I was like, "Damn,
I could die doing what I do."


01:21:56.131 --> 01:21:57.970
I remember tripping
just being like


01:21:57.970 --> 01:22:00.168
"Please God, like, don't let
me die riding today."


01:22:00.168 --> 01:22:01.726
<i>It took a long time for riders</i>


01:22:01.726 --> 01:22:02.965
<i>to throw a leg over their bikes</i>


01:22:02.965 --> 01:22:04.763
<i> after Jeremy Lusk passed.</i>


01:22:04.763 --> 01:22:06.962
<i> But the sport's heart
is progression,</i>


01:22:06.962 --> 01:22:08.919
<i> an internal engine
of human desire</i>


01:22:08.919 --> 01:22:10.438
<i> to test oneself</i>


01:22:10.438 --> 01:22:12.034
<i> and explore the unknown,</i>


01:22:12.034 --> 01:22:13.793
<i> and ride again, they did.</i>


01:22:13.793 --> 01:22:16.671
<i> I mean, you're talking
about X Games 1999,</i>


01:22:16.671 --> 01:22:19.508
<i> a backflip
was the biggest deal, ever.</i>


01:22:19.508 --> 01:22:22.066
Now, you're not even
getting to the--


01:22:22.066 --> 01:22:23.944
invited,
unless you do a backflip.


01:22:23.944 --> 01:22:25.701
<i> The double backflip proved</i>


01:22:25.701 --> 01:22:27.700
<i> that limits were only
what you couldn't think of,</i>


01:22:27.700 --> 01:22:29.938
<i> and progression continued.</i>


01:22:29.938 --> 01:22:32.215
<i> Chuck Carothers brought
a third-dimension</i>


01:22:32.215 --> 01:22:34.853
<i> to the sport by introducing
the body varial,</i>


01:22:34.853 --> 01:22:36.851
<i> which Kyle Loza would expand</i>


01:22:36.851 --> 01:22:40.048
<i> and refine to win three
consecutive gold medals.</i>


01:22:44.164 --> 01:22:46.123
<i>Aussie, Jackson "Jacko" Strong,</i>


01:22:46.123 --> 01:22:47.242
<i> who as a kid,
had been inspired</i>


01:22:47.242 --> 01:22:48.960
<i> by the Crusty movies</i>


01:22:48.960 --> 01:22:51.598
<i>and the theatrical Crusty Tour
that toured Down Under,</i>


01:22:51.598 --> 01:22:53.436
<i> showed that freestyle
could move forward</i>


01:22:53.436 --> 01:22:55.154
<i> by flipping the backflip</i>


01:22:55.154 --> 01:22:56.872
<i> and pulling a front flip.</i>


01:22:59.149 --> 01:23:00.628
<i>Fellow Aussie, Robbie Maddison</i>


01:23:00.628 --> 01:23:02.266
<i> became a force in the sport</i>


01:23:02.266 --> 01:23:04.264
<i> by not only pulling
cutting-edge tricks,</i>


01:23:04.264 --> 01:23:07.342
<i> but also setting
distance records.</i>


01:23:07.342 --> 01:23:09.259
<i> Freestyle expanded globally,</i>


01:23:09.259 --> 01:23:11.897
<i> inspiring riders like
Japan's Taka Higashino,</i>


01:23:11.897 --> 01:23:14.135
<i> who added perilous
technical difficulty</i>


01:23:14.135 --> 01:23:17.092
<i> to going upside down
with his backflip rock solid.</i>


01:23:20.089 --> 01:23:22.487
<i> Seth continued to jump
and set records,</i>


01:23:22.487 --> 01:23:24.444
<i> smashing his hero
Evel Knievel's record,</i>


01:23:24.444 --> 01:23:25.364
<i> on a Harley-Davidson</i>


01:23:25.364 --> 01:23:26.362
<i> by going by a hundred</i>


01:23:26.362 --> 01:23:27.802
<i> and eighty-five feet.</i>


01:23:27.802 --> 01:23:29.480
<i> He also reached
his own lifelong goal,</i>


01:23:29.480 --> 01:23:31.598
<i> going over 300 feet.</i>


01:23:31.598 --> 01:23:32.637
<i> A distance Evel himself</i>


01:23:32.637 --> 01:23:35.035
<i> thought was impossible.</i>


01:23:35.035 --> 01:23:38.033
<i>Three hundred
and one feet!</i>


01:23:40.989 --> 01:23:42.749
<i>When Seth Enslow
is not working</i>


01:23:42.749 --> 01:23:45.304
<i> as a contractor, he does
Spoken Word Poetry tours</i>


01:23:45.304 --> 01:23:46.623
<i> in Australia.</i>


01:23:46.623 --> 01:23:48.981
<i> And meets lots
of kids named, Seth.</i>


01:23:50.819 --> 01:23:53.257
<i> Brian Deegan continues
to win X Games medals</i>


01:23:53.257 --> 01:23:55.134
<i> in rally cars
and off road trucks,</i>


01:23:55.134 --> 01:23:56.974
<i>and is raising three children.</i>


01:23:58.731 --> 01:24:01.848
<i>Mike Metzger has set a world record!</i>


01:24:01.848 --> 01:24:03.806
<i> Mike Metzger is raising two children,</i>


01:24:03.806 --> 01:24:06.125
<i> teaching motocross,
and working as an artist</i>


01:24:06.125 --> 01:24:08.122
<i> while doing
professional tattoos.</i>


01:24:10.320 --> 01:24:12.119
<i> Carey Hart
has come full circle</i>


01:24:12.119 --> 01:24:14.836
<i> and owns an AMA Supercross
racing team</i>


01:24:14.836 --> 01:24:18.472
<i> and is raising his daughter
with his wife, Pink.</i>


01:24:18.472 --> 01:24:20.590
<i> Travis Pastrana
now tours the globe</i>


01:24:20.590 --> 01:24:23.508
<i> with his Nitro Circus
Action Sports Show,</i>


01:24:23.508 --> 01:24:25.385
<i> and is raising two children.</i>


01:24:27.864 --> 01:24:30.540
<i> And in 2015,
he would find himself</i>


01:24:30.540 --> 01:24:33.657
<i> as the catalyst for
the Next Great Leap Forward.</i>


01:24:33.657 --> 01:24:34.857
<i> This time, as a mentor,</i>


01:24:34.857 --> 01:24:36.535
<i> helping Aussie, Josh Sheehan</i>


01:24:36.535 --> 01:24:39.731
<i> prove once again
that the seemingly impossible,</i>


01:24:39.731 --> 01:24:43.368
<i> the seemingly suicidal,
is possible indeed.</i>


01:24:52.040 --> 01:24:55.157
<i> A triple backflip
on a motorcycle.</i>

